     "text": "```python\nfrom pedantic import rename_kwargs, retry, timer_class\n\n@timer_class\n@rename_kwargs\n@retry\nclass KthLargestFinder:\n    def __init__(self, nums: list, k: int):\n        self.nums = nums\n        self.k = k\n        self.sorted_nums = self._sort_nums()\n\n    def _sort_nums(self) -> list:\n        \"\"\"Sorts the list in ascending order.\"\"\"\n        return sorted(self.nums)\n\n    def find_kth_largest(self) -> int:\n        \"\"\"Returns the kth largest element in the array.\"\"\"\n        if not self.nums or self.k <= 0:\n            raise ValueError(\"Invalid input: nums must not be empty and k must be positive.\")\n        if self.k > len(self.nums):\n            raise ValueError(\"k cannot be larger than the length of the array.\")\n        \n        # Use a min-heap of size k to find the kth largest element\n        import heapq\n        return heapq.nlargest(self.k, self.nums)[-1]\n```",
